From 76a953fbe297824bc276b380d9a966a4adca4591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Agent <hermes-agent@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:18:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/23] fix(kanban): preserve declared home for identity
 workers

An allowlisted alias can lack a local profile directory, but spawning with -p default may redirect its worker away from the declaring HERMES_HOME. Validate the configured identity before selecting a lock, preserve the declaring home through CLI pre-parsing, and prefer an existing real profile. Invalid or malformed identity config falls back to legacy singleton locking; no database schema change.

Per-lane isolation still depends on dispatch_profiles. Identity-scoped and legacy gateways use different lock namespaces; coordinate a gateway restart during rollout and after rollback.

Verification on the identical source tree: focused tests 63 passed; broader Kanban tests 98 passed, 1 skipped; 10 repository guards and three fresh-CLI subprocess smoke cases passed. Pinned Ruff 0.15.10 health check was unavailable; no live rollout was performed.
